# boringssl.bot -- the package `boringssl`: one pinned BoringSSL as a link
# provider (HTTP-CLIENT-PACKAGE-MILESTONE-1.md, "The provider"). It declares
# the provider's archives, and nothing else: a package whose native code
# calls BoringSSL (the `http` package's unit) depends on this one and
# imports it, and an application's dependency graph holds one instance of
# it, so every such package links the same archives, once.
#
# The archive is BoringSSL's release tag 0.20261020.0 (commit d3bf4795, the
# PIN file), upstream's CMake build, unpatched and unprefixed: the members of
# libcrypto.a and libssl.a in one archive of its own name,
# libbotlish_boringssl.a, which no other library of the system (a
# distribution's OpenSSL) can stand in for. It also holds the provider's
# identity symbol (native/identity.c), which a unit compiled against these
# headers references: another provider fails the link. libssl is C++: its
# exception runtime is the system's libstdc++ (a system library the package
# declares).
#
# Native programs only, on the package's targets (Linux x86-64).
extern c library "botlish_boringssl" static at "native/libbotlish_boringssl.a"
extern c library "stdc++"

# The provider's identity: its tag and commit.
fn pin() -> str:
    "boringssl 0.20261020.0 d3bf4795ad5b79d646cddf2fec687da5b9b502db"
